{"id":"u-abd67158-9966-468d-a213-b58d4dd958d2","src":"community","title":"Science and Development of Muscle (Woman)","author":"Josmar Saiefert","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/sySIJN-science-and-development-of-muscle-hypertrophy-1","desc":"To provide a high-efficiency resistance training protocol for women aged 40+, specifically designed to counter age-related muscle loss (sarcopenia) and anabolic resistance. It uses evidence-based volume (10-20 sets per muscle/week) and supersets to maximize results in sessions under 50 minutes.\n\nTraining Structure: Full-Body Efficiency (3x Week)\nFrequency: 3 non-consecutive days per week (e.g., Monday, Wednesday, Friday).\nMethod: Antagonist Supersets (perform '1A' and then '1B' before resting).\nIntensity of Effort: Maintain 1-2 Repetitions in Reserve (RIR)\n\nNotes:\nEfficiency through Supersets: Using supersets allows you to complete more work in less time without compromising the hypertrophic stimulus.\nRecovery Management: Women in the 40-50 age range must prioritize the 48 to 72-hour recovery window between sessions for the same muscle group to allow for adequate tissue repair and avoid overtraining.\nProtein and the Leucine Threshold: To optimize results, ensure a protein intake of 1.8 to 2.2 g/kg. Older adults may require higher doses per meal (up to 40g) to overcome anabolic resistance and trigger muscle protein synthesis.\nFull Range of Motion (ROM): Ensure every exercise is performed through its full range of motion, as the stretched position of the muscle is a potent trigger for hypertrophy.\nProgression: As the 12th repetition becomes easier (RIR increases), increase the load to maintain the stimulus within the 8-12 rep range.","level":["Intermediate","Novice"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-06-06T00:44:25.268Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Full-Body Efficiency"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{